## Current roadmap / platform inheritance

GitHub #78 and `docs/MESSENGER_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE.md` are current authority. Existing domain/security rules remain valid.

Add content-free observability for WebSocket connections/reconnects, outbox backlog, sync cursor lag/pages, push failures and installation/device lifecycle. Never log E2EE plaintext or sensitive push contents.


# Observability and incident rules

- Use structured logs with correlation/request IDs.
- Redact cookies, authorization, passwords, API keys, OTP/recovery tokens and sensitive content.
- Important AI/billing operations log safe identifiers and result/status, not prompts/responses.
- Distinguish application logs, security/admin audit logs and append-only financial ledger.
- Financial/provider anomalies must be discoverable and reconciliation-ready.
- Preserve provider request ID, internal request ID, model/price version, usage and provider actual cost where relevant.
- Add metrics/alerts hooks for 5xx rate, auth failures, payment failures, provider failures, AI burn, queue backlog, DB latency and financial anomalies.
- Do not silently swallow unexpected failures. Return stable user error and emit operator-visible diagnostic context.
- Dangerous admin actions must record actor/target/action/result and before/after metadata where safe.
